(98, 3, 4, 65, '<p>John divided his property among his three sons- Tom, Dick and Harry. Harry&rsquo;s son Mathew had some dispute with Dick&rsquo;s son. Mathew&rsquo;s son Ivan helped in solving the dispute later. State the relation between Ivan and John.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 797, 0, 0, NULL),
(99, 3, 5, 66, '<p>What is V&rsquo;s profession?</p>\r\n', '<p>P, Q, R, S, T, V and W are travelling in three different vehicles. There are at least two passengers in each vehicle I, II &amp; III and only one of them is a male. There are two engineers, two doctors and three teachers among them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i) R is a lady doctor and she does not travel with the pair of sisters P and V.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ii) Q, a male engineer, travels only with W a teacher in vehicle I.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iii) S is a male doctor</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iv) Two person belonging to the same profession do not travel in the same vehicle.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>v) P is not an engineer and travels in vehicle II.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 800, 0, 0, NULL),
(100, 3, 5, 66, '<p>In which vehicle R does travel?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 805, 0, 0, NULL),
(101, 3, 5, 66, '<p>Which of the following represents the teacher?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 808, 0, 0, NULL),
