(139, 2, 5, 88, '<p>JEALOUS</p>\r\n', '<p>Choose the one which can be substituted for the given words/ sentence/ idiom and phrases&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 961, 0, 0, NULL),
(140, 2, 5, 88, '<p>EXEMPT</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 965, 0, 0, NULL),
(141, 2, 4, 89, '<p>I will meet you in &shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;&shy;__________</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 967, 0, 0, NULL),
(143, 2, 4, 90, '<p>The animals quickly ____________ to the environment.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 975, 0, 0, NULL),
(144, 2, 5, 91, '<p>God is present everywhere. He is _________</p>\r\n', '<p>In the question given below, choose the alternative one which can be most effectively substituted for the given word/ sentence.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 980, 0, 0, NULL),
(145, 2, 5, 91, '<p>A person who works very hard and finds it difficult to stop working.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 986, 0, 0, NULL),
(146, 2, 5, 92, '<p>Every Jack has a Jill.</p>\r\n', '<p>What the following phrase/ idiom/ proverb mean?</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 989, 0, 0, NULL),
(147, 2, 5, 92, '<p>To get into hot water</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 992, 0, 0, NULL),
(148, 2, 2, 93, '<p>Choose the correct word to fill in the blank.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Place the pen ________ the notebook.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 996, 0, 0, NULL),
(149, 2, 4, 94, '<p>Choose the option that is the most appropriate synonym to the given word.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>CANDOUR</strong></p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1000, 0, 0, NULL),
(150, 3, 4, 95, '<p>Which of the following is a couple?</p>\r\n', '<p>Read the following passage and answer the question following</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i) A, B, C, D, E and F are six members of a family.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ii) There are two couples in the family.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iii) C is the mother of A and F.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iv) E is the father of D.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>v) A is the grandson of B.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>vi) There are total 3 ladies in the family.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 1005, 0, 0, NULL),
(151, 3, 4, 95, '<p>Who is the wife of E?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1007, 0, 0, NULL),
(153, 3, 4, 95, '<p>How is B related to F?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1016, 0, 0, NULL),
(154, 3, 4, 95, '<p>How is F related to A?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1022, 0, 0, NULL),
(155, 3, 4, 95, '<p>Which of the following are ladies?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1026, 0, 0, NULL),
(156, 3, 2, 96, '<p>Who is facing towards A?</p>\r\n', '<p>A, B, C, D, E and F are sitting in a circle facing towards the center. D is between F and B. A is second to the left of D and second to the right of E.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 1029, 0, 0, NULL),
(157, 3, 2, 96, '<p>Who is facing towards D?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1031, 0, 0, NULL),
(158, 3, 2, 97, '<p>In each of the questions below are given few statements followed by few conclusions numbered. Considering the given statements to be true, read all conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusion logically follow the given statement.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Statements </em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(i) No man is sky</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) No sky is road</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(iii) Some men are road</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Conclusions</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(I) No road is man</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(II) No road is sky</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(III) Some skies are men</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(IV) All roads are men</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1038, 0, 0, NULL),
(159, 3, 2, 98, '<p>Anil, introducing a girl in a party said she is the wife of the grandson of my mother. How is Anil related to the girl?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1044, 0, 0, NULL),
(161, 3, 2, 99, '<p>If E=5, PEN=35, then PAGER=?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1047, 0, 0, NULL),
(162, 3, 2, 100, '<p>If Z=52 and ACT=48, then BAT will be equal to?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1054, 0, 0, NULL),
(163, 3, 2, 101, '<p>Find the missing no.</p>\n\n<p><img alt="" src="http://202.129.196.133/aptitudetest/public/images/Screenshot from 2019-04-26 15-18-24.png" style="height:109px; width:583px" /></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</p>\n', NULL, 'No', 1, 1057, 0, 0, NULL),
(165, 3, 2, 102, '<p>Which of these is the odd one out?&nbsp;</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<p>0&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;8&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;28&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 48&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 80</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1065, 0, 0, NULL),
(166, 3, 2, 103, '<p>Find the Odd one out?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1070, 0, 0, NULL),
(167, 3, 4, 104, '<p>Who is the tallest?</p>\r\n', '<p>Read the following to answer the questions that follow</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Jayesh is taller than Mohan, but shorter than Ashok. Shashi is taller than Mohan but shorter than Vijay</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 1073, 0, 0, NULL),
(168, 3, 4, 104, '<p>Who is the shortest?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1078, 0, 0, NULL),
(169, 3, 4, 105, '<p>Now in what direction is he from the start point?</p>\r\n', '<p>Rajesh moved 6Km to east and then moved 10Km after turning to his right. He then moved 6Km after turning to his right. Again he moved 15Km after turning to his left. Now in what direction and how far is he from the start point.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 1079, 0, 0, NULL),
(170, 3, 4, 105, '<p>How far is he from the start point?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1085, 0, 0, NULL),
(171, 3, 2, 106, '<p>10, 25, 45, 54,60,75,80</p>\r\n', '<p>Find the odd one out.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 1089, 0, 0, NULL),
(172, 3, 2, 106, '<p>5, 10, 17, 26, 50</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1094, 0, 0, NULL),
(177, 3, 4, 107, '<p>&nbsp;Select from alternative, the box that can be formed by folding the sheet down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt="" src="http://202.129.196.133/aptitudetest/public/images/Screenshot from 2019-04-08 13-42-05.png" style="height:147px; width:231px" /> A)&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://202.129.196.133/aptitudetest/public/images/Screenshot from 2019-04-08 13-42-18.png" style="height:75px; width:73px" />&nbsp; &nbsp;B)&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://202.129.196.133/aptitudetest/public/images/Screenshot from 2019-04-08 13-42-34.png" style="height:74px; width:78px" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n', NULL, 'No', 1, 1112, 0, 0, NULL),
(179, 2, 4, 108, '<p>In the following sentence four words or phrases have been underlined. Only one underlined part in each sentence is not acceptable, pick up the part a, b, c or d.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt="" src="http://202.129.196.133/aptitudetest/public/images/Screenshot from 2019-04-22 18-35-23.png" style="height:82px; width:555px" /></p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 1135, 0, 0, NULL);
